 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Chinese President Xi Jinping greets President Trump today in Shenzhen, China. Photo: Mandel Ngan/AFP via Getty Images 🇺🇸 🇷🇺 President Trump plans to meet separately with Russian President Vladimir Putin tomorrow in China, in addition to their already scheduled three-way meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping. More from Barak Ravid . ✈️ Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin defended his weekend flight to a college football game as many travelers were still stuck after Friday's nationwide ground stop. He told a House committee that canceling his trip could have caused confusion. Go deeper . 🇻🇪 Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth is visiting Venezuela to meet with interim authorities, underscoring the Trump administration's efforts to deepen its influence there. Go deeper . House Minority Leader Hakeem Jeffries embraces House Democratic Whip Katherine Clark (D-Mass.) after today's vote. Photo: Aaron Schwartz/Reuters 🏛️ Democrats voted at a closed-door caucus meeting this morning to nominate Minority Leader Hakeem Jeffries (D-N.Y.) as their candidate for speaker, Axios' Andrew Solender reports. 

 It's a symbolic but significant step that suggests Jeffries has the votes to be elected the first Black House speaker on Jan. 3. Go deeper . 
 
